course: dictionary
lesson: 6842
title: Outlive: living longer, or lasting longer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To outlive someone means to live longer than them. «A pet parrot may outlive its owner» means the parrot could still be alive after its owner has died.
explain: The word has a second meaning, for things. Something outlives its purpose when it keeps going after it has stopped being useful. «The rule has outlived its purpose» means the rule is still there, but it no longer does the job it was made for.
explain: Context gives you the clues. Look at what the sentence is about: is it about living things, like parrots and tortoises, or about rules and machines? That tells you which meaning fits. Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: Outlive means to live longer than someone else.
fact: Outlive can also mean to last longer than something, or to keep going after it has stopped being useful.
fact: «Some parrots live for over 60 years, so a pet parrot may outlive its owner.»
fact: «A tortoise can outlive its owner's whole family.»
fact: Jonathan, a tortoise on the island of St Helena, is thought to have hatched around 1832.
exercise: «Some parrots live for over 60 years, so a pet parrot may outlive its owner.» What does outlive mean here? | *To live longer than someone else | To learn to talk | To be fed and walked every day | To live in the same house
exercise: «The rule has outlived its purpose.» What does this suggest? | The rule has been broken many times | The rule was written only last week | *The rule still exists but no longer does its job | The rule makes everyone very happy
exercise: Which animal in the lessons can outlive its owner's whole family? | A cat | A hamster | *A tortoise | A mayfly
test: Which word means to live longer than someone else? | Outline | *Outlive | Outgrow | Outdoor
test: «A hamster is old at 2, a cat often lives 12 to 18 years, and a tortoise can live even longer.» Which pet lives longest? | A hamster | *A tortoise | A cat
exam: Which sentence uses outlive to mean something lasted after it stopped being useful? | The old map was folded in half. | The old map was left outdoors. | *The old map outlived its purpose. | The old map was outlined in red.
